<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.12.6: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01942</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.12.6: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>d7001c44-0018-49c9-9320-540971232290</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para><emphasis><emphasis>Students will complete the following questions to practice the skills they have learned in this lesson.</emphasis></emphasis></para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>Choose the quadratic equation that is represented by the graph.</item>
</list>
<para><figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/bd59d8abb03c9dac56adad4cf8fd4dc0d9bf2f64"/></media></figure></para>
<list>
  <item> \(f(x)=x^2+5\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x)=x^2-3\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x)=x^2\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x)=x^2+7\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(f(x)=x^2-3\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>Choose the quadratic equation that is represented by the graph.</item>
</list>
<para><figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/adfa84a6542f9a442bd0985740fca99dde05c3fe"/></media></figure></para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \(f(x)=x^2+5\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x)=x^2-3\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x)=x^2\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x)=x^2+7\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(f(x)=x^2\) </para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>Choose the quadratic equation that is represented by the graph.</item>
</list>
<para><figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/db8c1a97b5b5d84b10453c8245ae8f09992c8ff9"/></media></figure></para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \(f(x)=x^2+5\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x)=x^2-3\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x)=x^2\) </item>
  <item>\(f(x)=x^2+7\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis>\(f(x)=x^2+7\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item>Choose the quadratic equation that is represented by the graph.</item>
</list>
<para><figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/cd72afad226904dbabcd17ff4213295c0c300836"/></media></figure></para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \(f(x)=x^2+5\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x)=x^2-3\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x)=x^2\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x)=x^2+7\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(f(x)=x^2+5\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
  <item>The following two equations are equivalent.</item>
</list>
<para>factored form \(f(x)=(x+2)(x+3)\) 
  standard form \(f(x)=x^2+5x+6\) </para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item> Which equation helps find the \(x\)-intercepts most efficiently? </item>
</list>
<list>
  <item> factored form </item>
  <item> standard form </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> factored form</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item> Which equation helps find the \(y\)-intercept most efficiently? </item>
</list>
<list>
  <item> factored form </item>
  <item> standard form </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> standard form</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
  <item> There are three equations represented on this graph:</item>
</list>
<para>\(f(x)=x^2\) (black graph, at the top, opening upward)
  \(f(x)=x^2-4\)
  \(f(x)=-x^2+5\)</para>
<para>Use the graph to answer questions a and b.</para>
<para><figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/f02a214586d1dccfe80f82e0a2c83c4656637b78"/></media></figure></para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item> Which graph represents the equation \(f(x)=x^2-4\)? </item>
</list>
<list>
  <item> Green graph (at the bottom, opening downward) </item>
  <item> Blue graph (in the middle, opening upward) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Blue graph (in the middle, opening upward)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item> Which graph represents the equation \(f(x)=-x^2+5\)? </item>
</list>
<list>
  <item> Green graph (at the bottom, opening downward) </item>
  <item> Blue graph (in the middle, opening upward) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Green graph (at the bottom, opening downward)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="7" type="enumerated">
  <item> <emphasis>Select two</emphasis> equations whose graphs have a positive \(y\)-intercept. </item>
</list>
<list>
  <item> \(f(x)=x^2+3x-2\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x)=x^2-10x\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x)=(x-1)^2\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x)=5x^2-3x-5\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x)=(x+1)(x+2)\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(f(x)=(x-1)^2\), \(f(x)=(x+1)(x+2)\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="8" type="enumerated">
  <item>Which function represents the graph of \(f(x)=x^2\) shifted 5 units to the right?  </item>
</list>
<list>
  <item> \(f(x)=x^2+5\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x)=x^2-5\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x)=(x+5)^2\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x)=(x-5)^2\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(f(x)=(x-5)^2\) </para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="9" type="enumerated">
  <item><emphasis>Select three</emphasis> equations whose graphs open downward.</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item>\(f(x)=(1-x)^2\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x)=1-x^2\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x)=-(x-1)^2\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x)=-1+x^2\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x)=(1-x)(x+2)\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>\(f(x)=1-x^2\), \(f(x)=-(x-1)^2\), \(f(x)=(1-x)(x+2)\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="10" type="enumerated">
  <item>Which curve is the narrowest?</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item>\(f(x)=3x^2\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x)=(3x)^2\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x)=\frac{1}{3}x^2\) </item>
  <item>\( f(x)=(\frac{1}{3}x)^2\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(f(x)=(3x)^2\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="11" type="enumerated">
  <item>Which equation is represented by the graph?</item>
</list>
<para><figure><media alt=""><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/fc657952ff3dc0167c3490f2019580516f49e586"/></media></figure></para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \(f(x)=(x-4)^2+4\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x)=(x+4)^2+4\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x)=-(x-4)^2+4\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x)=-(x+4)^2+4\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(f(x)=-(x-4)^2+4\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="12" type="enumerated">
  <item>Which equation is represented by the graph?</item>
</list>
<para><figure><media alt="Graph on coordinate plane. Horizontal axis by twos from negative 8 to 8. Vertical axis by twos from negative 4 to 8. Graph goes through point 0 comma 7."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/0c9e5c47508f4c799bd5a6d9399b43a536189bb2"/></media></figure></para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \(f(x)=(x-2)^2+3\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x)=(x-3)^2+2\) </item>
  <item> \(f(x)=(x+2)^2+3\) </item>
  <item>\( f(x)=(x+3)^2+2\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>\(f(x)=(x+2)^2+3\)</para>
<para>For questions 13 - 14, use the following graph. </para>
<para><figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/07e59d96075a1ea4852d468146010b7fdf6385e8"/></media></figure></para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="13" type="enumerated">
  <item>Which of the graphs has been horizontally stretched? </item>
</list>
<list>
  <item>Graph a</item>
  <item>Graph b</item>
  <item>Graph c</item>
  <item>Graph d</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Graph d </para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="14" type="enumerated">
  <item>Which function most closely represents the equation for graph c?</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item>\(f(x) = (x - 2.5)^2\)</item>
  <item>\(f(x) = (4x)^2\)</item>
  <item>\(f(x) = (x + 2.5)^2\)</item>
  <item>\(f(x) = (\frac14x)^2\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(f(x) = (x - 2.5)^2\)</para> </section>
</content>
